---
description: Investigate the owned image evidence relevant to the requested decision, retaining actual readbacks and uncertainty.
budget: { maxTurns: 32 }
args:
  goal: string
returns: ImageInvestigation
---
Choose the investigations needed to understand the user's image request. Discover actual owned briefs and use the brief-selection branch when useful. Retain the real selection scope, observed journals and original readbacks. The assessment branch can judge which candidates deserve original inspection from the actual evidence history; it is an internal plan, not proof that any original is usable.

Read the candidates that matter to the requested current, historical or comparison outcome. A refused or unavailable read is a finding to reason about, not a reason to invent successful bytes. Refresh when a changed frontier, selection, rights or attempt matters; a fixed number of reads is not evidence of freshness. Preserve distinct native candidate identities, owner, source receipt, exact reference and observed media format. Keep the complete actual original readback objects. If no owned brief can be established, return a null plan and the limits discovered. Do not stage or dispatch anything in this investigation.
